  "details": "Some problems I see with it are:\n\n1. The icon, status, username and pronouns are all on the same line, with equal emphasis on each of them. Ideally, the icon on the old nameplate was layed out better. Your status was also layed out better, being BELOW your username. Your username should be the focus, being the biggest, and should have its own line. Your pronouns should also have its own little area so people can see it better.\n\n2. Group banners now get hidden even more than they did before, so now its even harder to have a group banner to actually show for everyone else without them opening their quick menu.\n\n3. The outline of the nameplate being yellow instead of the username being yellow for your friends is a lot harder to notice at a glance, as well as it being hard to tell when someone is speaking or not.\n\n4. The nameplates are just too big by default. They take up so much space on your screen, and they are harder on the eyes in comparison.\n\nIm not a fan of the new nameplates. The current one couldve just been touched up a bit instead, eg: new gradient, moved icons, etc.",
